# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# JossPaperAR — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
#
# Two rules that follow from ADR-001 (Expo/RN + Supabase + hosted AI) and
# ADR-005 (honest client):
#   1. Only variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ are ever exposed to the app bundle.
#      Anything else travels to the device. Treat every EXPO_PUBLIC_ value as
#      public — no secrets, no AI API keys.
#   2. Server-side secrets live in `supabase/functions/.env` (local) or
#      `supabase secrets set` (hosted) — never here. Supabase also INJECTS
#      SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SECRET_KEYS / etc. into Edge Functions, so the
#      service-role key is never something you set by hand.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Supabase (app-facing) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project: yercgevebxvtzkgctfai  ·  region ap-southeast-1 (Singapore)  ·  Postgres 17.11
# This is the PUBLISHABLE key (`sb_publishable_…`). It is designed to be public:
# it ships inside the app bundle and is protected by Row Level Security, not by
# secrecy. It replaces the legacy `anon` key (which still works until end-2026).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://yercgevebxvtzkgctfai.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The modern name for the same value is also read (it is preferred in new code):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_…
# src/lib/supabase.ts accepts EITHER name, so an older `.env` keeps working.

# ── Optional: pointing the app at a local dev backend ───────────────────────
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:54321

# ── Server-side secrets live in a DIFFERENT file ────────────────────────────
# Not here. See `supabase/functions/.env.example`:
#   local  → supabase/functions/.env                (auto-loaded by `supabase start`)
#   hosted → supabase secrets set --env-file supabase/functions/.env
#
# ⚠️ Do NOT try to set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY / SUPABASE_SECRET_KEYS yourself.
# Supabase INJECTS them into every Edge Function, and any name starting with
# SUPABASE_ is reserved. The service-role/secret key never goes in any file here.
